Doc no. DER-EQP-SOC-PTOH · Rev — · Date 07/14/2025 · Owner SOC Shift Supervisor	
Register	SOC PTO-Hold Log — refusals of Permission to Operate on telemetry grounds
Maintained by	Lena Kovalchuk, SOC Shift Supervisor (lena.kovalchuk@alleniom.com)
As of	07/14/2025
Standing note	
No PTO without live telemetry — TCS-02 §5 (no interim provision). All entries below are in-scope DER sites (≥500 kW) at which the utility-owned RTU is not physically installed, not commissioned end-to-end per TCS-02 §3.6, and not presenting valid points at the SCADA operator display. PTO is refused under TCS-02 §5 until the telemetry condition is satisfied. This log is refreshed on the SOC shift turnover cycle.	
SOC Notes	
1.	All seven sites are construction-complete and are held out of service until utility-owned RTU install, end-to-end commissioning per TCS-02 §3.6, and valid points at SCADA per TCS-02 §6.
2.	TCS-02 §5 contains no interim provision. Absence of an interim clause is absence, not a stated exception. Requests for early, provisional, partial, or conditional operation are refused on the same basis and returned to the DER Program Office.
3.	Equipment supply and deployment sequencing are tracked by the DER Program Office (see companion register DER-EQP-COMPL, Completed Sites Awaiting Utility Equipment) and by SCADA/EMS Engineering (Marcus Deele). SOC does not sequence equipment; SOC confirms live telemetry at the moment PTO is requested.
4.	Requesting-party entries are transcribed from the written PTO request on file. Priority claims received from stakeholders are not tracked in this log; they are captured on DER-EQP-COMPL.
5.	Rows remain open until telemetry is confirmed live. Closure is logged against the interconnection file with SOC operator initials and timestamp.
Prepared by: Lena Kovalchuk, SOC Shift Supervisor — 07/14/2025.	
